# Walkthrough: Spotify Player & Configuration Fixes

I have resolved the issues affecting the Spotify integration, including the 404 error, the `TypeError` in token refresh, and the 500 Internal Server Error during the callback.

## Changes Made

### Backend

- **[spotify.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/routers/spotify.py)**:
    - **Fixed 404/TypeError**: Standardized all datetime comparisons to use naive UTC via `lib.timezone.now_utc()` instead of `datetime.now(UTC)`.
    - **Fixed 500 Error**: Resolved a `NameError` in [spotify_callback](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/routers/spotify.py#50-104) where `UTC` was being used but was not imported.
    - Verified the backend is correctly registering the Spotify router.

### Frontend

- **[SpotifyPlayer.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/components/SpotifyPlayer.tsx)**:
    - Updated the "Configuration Required" message to point you to **Settings > Integrations** instead of the `.env` file.

## Verification Results

### Automated Tests
- Verified `/api/v1/spotify/me` returns 401 (Correct) instead of 404.
- Code review confirmed [now_utc()](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/lib/timezone.py#11-14) is used consistently, avoiding `TypeError` and `NameError`.

### Manual Verification
- The login flow should now proceed without a 500 error after you enter your credentials and Spotify redirects back to the app.
